-- CK-159's refusing half (R15-fix-E): `H.eq` is specialised to `Holder Int`,
-- so a type that holds a `Holder a` derives `==` only at `a = Int` — its
-- context PINS the parameter (checker-v2.md §11.2 *as amended by
-- R15-fix-E*). At any other argument it is NOT EQUATABLE, and the message
-- writes the type as it derives: through an imported row (`M.W`, whose
-- published scheme carries the pin, so it cannot name `H.eq`), a local type
-- (`Y`, which names it), a pin inherited through another local type (`Z`),
-- a rigid argument, and inside a list. The accepting half is
-- `run/DerivedPinnedAcrossModules` and `run/DerivedOverSpecialisedEq`.
pub type Holder a
    = Holder a


pub eq : Holder Int, Holder Int -> Bool
eq (Holder x) (Holder y) =
    modBy x 10 == modBy y 10
